=====================================================================================
 BONUS B6  CONDITIONALS IN A VIEW: @if / else     Pointer 5: Razor Views
=====================================================================================

 LESSON
 ------
 You've used @foreach. The other Razor power tool is @if: show HTML only when a condition is true.
 An else branch covers the other case. A nice combo is a loop inside a loop: for each doctor,
 loop that doctor's patients, but if there are none, say so instead of showing an empty box.

 WORKED EXAMPLE (each Author with their Books)
 ---------------------------------------------
   @model IEnumerable<LibraryApp.Models.Author>

   @foreach (var author in Model)
   {
       <h4>@author.Name</h4>

       @if (author.Books.Any())
       {
           <ul>
               @foreach (var book in author.Books)
               {
                   <li>@book.Title</li>
               }
           </ul>
       }
       else
       {
           <p>No books yet.</p>
       }
   }

 Any() asks "is there at least one item?" (it comes from LINQ and is already available in views).

 COMMON TRAPS
 ------------
 * In Razor, the C# keyword else follows the closing brace of the @if on its own: } else { ... }
   Don't put an @ in front of else.
 * If the controller did not Include() the Patients, author.Books is null and Any() explodes (B3).
 * Inside a code block, HTML must be wrapped in a tag. Plain text needs a tag like <p>.

 THE TASK
 --------
 Write the Razor view for the Doctors Index page:
   [B6] model = IEnumerable of Doctor (HospitalApp.Models.Doctor)
   [B6] loop over the doctors and show each doctor's Name
   [B6] with @if: when doctor.Patients has any patients, loop over them (nested foreach) and show
        each FullName; otherwise show a "no patients" message using else.

 HINT
 ----
 The Doctor class has a Patients collection. The controller that feeds this view is B3.
 Seeded data (B2) gives you doctors with and without patients to see both branches.

 >>>>> WRITE YOUR ANSWER BELOW THIS LINE <<<<<
*@
@model IEnumerable<HospitalApp.Models.Doctor>

<h2>Doctors</h2>

@foreach (var doctor in Model)
{
    <h4>@doctor.Name</h4>

    @if (doctor.Patients.Any())
    {
        <ul>
            @foreach (var patient in doctor.Patients)
            {
                <li>@patient.FullName</li>
            }
        </ul>
    }
    else
    {
        <p>No patients yet.</p>
    }
}
